# Only build intermediates and bytecode are ignored. Documents are tracked,
# including the .docx that build/build_docs.py generates from doc/specs/*.md, so that a
# reader without pandoc -- a reviewer, or the instructor -- can open a
# specification straight from the repository.
#
# The trade-off that comes with that, stated so nobody is surprised by it:
# doc/specs/*.md remains the source of truth, and a committed .docx can fall behind
# its markdown if somebody edits the source without rebuilding. Nothing detects
# that, because .docx is a zip whose bytes change on every build even when the
# content does not, so a regenerate-and-compare check like the one guarding
# qnsc_pkg.sv is not possible here. Rebuild before committing:
#
#     make docs

# Build intermediate: the numbering-stripped reference document that
# build_docs.py derives from the template on each run.
build/template/QNSC_Reference_NoAutoNum.docx

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
